From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: small discarded buffers staged without asking whether they are busy

Patch 0034 sends discard maps of buffers up to 64 KB through the staging buffer when the buffer is busy, which it
asked the kernel each time (an escape, ~3 us; ~5000 a second in 3DMark Vantage). The staging path costs less than
the question: such maps take it busy or not.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
@@ -223,18 +223,19 @@ virgl_resource_transfer_prepare(struct virgl_context *vctx,
       assert(!readback);
 
       if (can_realloc || vctx->supports_staging) {
+         /* Small buffers (constant buffers, small dynamic vertex/index buffers) go through the staging buffer
+          * even where they could be reallocated: on Windows a new resource is a kernel allocation and a host
+          * resource every time, and a game discarding a constant buffer per draw spent ~5 us in each (D3D11
+          * Map(WRITE_DISCARD) per draw ran slower than WARP); the staging path is a suballocation and a copy the
+          * host does in order. They take it busy or not: asking costs a kernel call each (~3 us, thousands a
+          * second), more than the staging copy */
+         bool small = res->b.target == PIPE_BUFFER && res->b.width0 <= 64 * 1024 && vctx->supports_staging &&
+                      !res->discard_realloc;
          /* Both map types have some costs.  Do them only when the resource is
           * (or will be) busy for real.  Otherwise, set wait to false.
           */
-         wait = (flush || vws->resource_is_busy(vws, res->hw_res));
+         wait = (small || flush || vws->resource_is_busy(vws, res->hw_res));
          if (wait) {
-            /* Small buffers (constant buffers, small dynamic vertex/index buffers) go through the staging buffer
-             * even where they could be reallocated: on Windows a new resource is a kernel allocation and a host
-             * resource every time, and a game discarding a constant buffer per draw spent ~5 us in each (D3D11
-             * Map(WRITE_DISCARD) per draw ran slower than WARP); the staging path is a suballocation and a copy the
-             * host does in order */
-            bool small = res->b.target == PIPE_BUFFER && res->b.width0 <= 64 * 1024 && vctx->supports_staging &&
-                         !res->discard_realloc;
             map_type = (can_realloc && !small) ?
                VIRGL_TRANSFER_MAP_REALLOC :
                VIRGL_TRANSFER_MAP_WRITE_TO_STAGING;
